<title>HONG KONG: Kosonic year net loss HK$284.18 mln.</title>
<headline>Kosonic year net loss HK$284.18 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 59.7 loss   vs 5.9 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	116.15 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			  284.18 loss vs 23.39 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		   935.72	vs 1,172.70</p>
<p>    Company name	     Kosonic International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		March 21 to April 2</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Kosonic International is a maker of compact disc audio systems.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on provision for closure of production facilities after the balance sheet date, stocks and work in progress written down to net realisable value and progress written off, lots arising from the difference between the value of stocks returned from debtors and the remaining balances of the debtors in the balance sheet whereas these balances represented goods sold to these debtors in the China in prior year.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
